---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout class="resume">
  <hgroup>
    <h1>Carter McBride</h1>
    <p>Software Engineer · Saratoga Springs, Utah</p>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:jobs@carter.works">jobs@carter.works</a> ·
      <a href="https://carter.works">carter.works</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/carterworks">github.com/carterworks</a> ·
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/thatcartermcbride/"
        >linkedin.com/in/thatcartermcbride</a
      >
    </p>
  </hgroup>

  <p>
    Web developer since 2016, now on Adobe’s open-source Web SDK. Likes small bundles, simple builds and tests worth
    trusting.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Experience</h2>

    <article>
      <h3>Software Engineer, Adobe <span>Jan 2022 – Present</span></h3>
      <p>Lehi, Utah</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Develop the Adobe Experience Platform Web SDK (<a
            href="https://github.com/adobe/alloy">adobe/alloy</a
          >), the open-source library enterprise sites use to collect data and
          personalize pages, plus its Tags extension and the Experience Platform
          Debugger.
        </li>
        <li>
          Cut typing lag in the Tags extension from 140–209 ms to under 15 ms per
          keystroke by rebuilding its forms on TanStack Form and ArkType, and
          moved its UI to React Spectrum 2.
        </li>
        <li>
          Cut the gzipped SDK by 9%, from 44 KB to 40 KB, by dropping Internet
          Explorer; added bundle-size reporting to CI and a browser-compatibility
          lint.
        </li>
        <li>
          Split the SDK into a platform-agnostic core and a browser package, and
          wrote the migration plan, as groundwork for a Node.js SDK.
        </li>
        <li>
          Moved the SDK into a pnpm monorepo and made its releases to npm and
          the CDN automatic and retry-safe with Changesets.
        </li>
        <li>
          Migrated 17 functional test suites from TestCafe to Vitest, Playwright
          and Mock Service Worker.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>
        Software Developer, ICE Mortgage Technology <span
          >Jan 2019 – Jan 2022</span
        >
      </h3>
      <p>Provo, Utah</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Improved performance of critical-path features, championed simpler
          workflows for large customers, and mentored new hires.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>Software Engineer, Lingotek <span>May 2018 – Dec 2018</span></h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Moved several pages of the main product to Vue.js, cutting page load
          times by 15%.
        </li>
        <li>
          Reworked a large project’s build, cutting build times by 25% and
          letting developers use modern tools.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>
        Front-End Web Developer, Brigham Young University <span
          >Feb 2016 – May 2018</span
        >
      </h3>
      <p>Provo, Utah</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Built features for Learning Suite, BYU’s learning management system,
          used by thousands; backed them with unit tests and automated
          developer setup.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Projects</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://yazzy.carter.works">Yazzy</a>: reader mode for any
        web article, in Astro.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/carterworks/substack-to-epub"
          >substack-to-epub</a
        >: saves a Substack newsletter to SQLite and formats it as an EPUB, in
        Python.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://carter.works">carter.works</a>: this site, with its
        pixel-art backdrop extracted into a self-contained web components package.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Education</h2>
    <h3>
      B.S. Computer Science, Brigham Young University <span>2015 – 2019</span>
    </h3>
    <p>
      Minor in Portuguese. Third place, BYU Google Games 2017.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Skills</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>Languages</dt>
      <dd>TypeScript, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Python, Go</dd>
      <dt>Web</dt>
      <dd>Web components, Astro, React, Vue.js, Node.js</dd>
      <dt>Tooling</dt>
      <dd>
        Vite, Rollup, Vitest, Playwright, pnpm, GitHub Actions, Claude Code
      </dd>
      <dt>Spoken</dt>
      <dd>English, Brazilian Portuguese</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(.resume) {
    --flow-space: var(--size-sm);

    display: grid;
    gap: var(--size-md);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 1.6em;
  }

  h2 {
    border-block-end: 1px solid;
    font-size: 1em;
    margin-block-end: var(--size-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h3 {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-size: 1em;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  h3 span {
    font-weight: normal;
  }

  article + article {
    margin-block-start: var(--size-sm);
  }

  ul {
    padding-inline-start: 1.2em;
  }

  dl {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0 var(--size-sm);
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
  }

  dt {
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  @media print {
    @page {
      margin: 0.5in;
      size: letter;
    }

    :global(html) {
      color-scheme: light;
      font-size: 10pt;
    }

    :global(body) {
      background: none;
      color: #000;
      display: block;
    }

    :global(pixel-backdrop),
    :global(body > .stack > header) {
      display: none;
    }

    :global(.resume) {
      background: none;
      gap: var(--size-sm);
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }

    a {
      color: inherit;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    a[href]::after {
      content: none;
    }
  }
</style>
